-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/judge.json:3:  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Across the 8 reviewed CMS Medicaid ex parte renewal-share traces, Brier generally identified the correct state-row resolver, used official CMS/data.medicaid.gov context, anchored forecasts in state-specific recent history, and incorporated pre-submit reviewer feedback into more auditable prior/update/interval explanations. The main system weaknesses are repeated: catalog lookups sometimes expose prior point/interval values that exactly match the final forecast and create circularity risk; the strict first-print original-submission resolver repeatedly drifted into same-release-day correction exceptions before review; sparse historical samples were used without a structured representation of missing months, vintage status, and volatility method; and high-ceiling percentage targets need a more standardized bounded-interval calibration. These are fixable with prompt changes, validators, and CMS-specific source adapter fields rather than case-by-case reviewer intervention.\\\",\\n./records/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/judge.json:20:        \\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\\\",\\n./records/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/judge.json:21:        \\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\n./records/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/judge.json:22:        \\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\n./records/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/judge.json:23:        \\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\n./records/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/judge.json:24:        \\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\n./records/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/judge.json:25:        \\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"\\n./records/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/judge.json:34:      