 release is scheduled for 25/06/2026 at 11:30am AEST, so the resolution date is 2026-06-25.\"\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2202392:            \"Forecast Australia May 2026 unemployment first print\",\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2202393:            \"Base-rate/reference-class: adjacent-month Australian unemployment prints usually move by 0.0 to 0.2 percentage points at one-decimal precision outside shocks. The latest four seasonally adjusted prints, 4.1, 4.3, 4.3, and 4.5, imply a level around the mid-4s, while the April trend estimate of 4.3 suggests not all of the April spike should be extrapolated.\"\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2202421:            \"Employment change is a fast, noisy target that helps calibrate household income, tax receipts, and welfare-demand predictions. This target resolves on 2026-06-25 under a first-print rule, with an expected ~3 weeks lag. The same series can also spawn next release, +3 months, unemployment threshold questions.\"\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2202431:            \"Employment change is a fast, noisy target that helps calibrate household income, tax receipts, and welfare-demand predictions. This target resolves on 2026-06-25 under a first-print rule, with an expected ~3 weeks lag. The same series can also spawn next release, +3 months, unemployment threshold questions.\"\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2202555:            \"Tool result: { admitted: 3, mode: \\\"with_packs\\\", required_checks: [\\\"employment_base_rate\\\",\\\"hours_worked\\\",\\\"unemployment_consistency\\\",\\\"survey_release_noise\\\"] }\"\nrecords/target-architecture/2026-06-29-projection.json:2202564:            \"Tool result: { admitted: 3, mode: \\\"with_packs\\\", required_checks: [\\\"employment_base_rate\\\",\\\"hours_worked\\\",\\\"unemployment_consistency\\\",\\\"survey_release_noise\\\"] }\"\nrecords/target-archit