s/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:3:    \"slug\": \"bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:6:    \"title\": \"US unemployment rate, June 2026\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:7:    \"question\": \"What will the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics report as the seasonally adjusted civilian unemployment rate, age 16 and over, for June 2026 in the first Employment Situation print?\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:16:    \"resolutionRule\": \"Resolve to the first BLS Employment Situation release value for the seasonally adjusted civilian unemployment rate, age 16 and over, for reference month June 2026, reported in percent to one decimal place. Use the initial July 2, 2026 print and ignore later revisions or annual population-control revisions.\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:17:    \"dataPointId\": \"bls.cps.unemployment_rate.2026-06.first_print\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:41:      \"Recent unemployment rate has been flat near 4.3 percent\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:57:        \"text\": \"Forecast for June 2026 BLS CPS unemployment rate\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:61:        \"text\": \"The resolver is the first official BLS Employment Situation print for June 2026, using the seasonally adjusted civilian unemployment rate for people age 16 and over, rounded to one decimal percent.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:73:        \"result\": \"BLS reported total nonfarm payroll employment increased by 172,000 in May and the unemployment rate was unchanged at 4.3 percent; unemployed people were 7.3 million.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:79:        \"result\": \"Seasonally adjusted unemployment rates in table A-1 were Jan 2026 4.3, Feb 2026 4.4, Mar 2026 4.3, Apr 2026 4.3, May 2026 4.3 percent.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:89:        \"text\": \"Base-rate/reference class: one-month moves in the rounded unemployment rate are usually small, and the immediate recent reference class is especially persistent: five latest monthly values are all between 4.3 and 4.4, with four of five at 4.3.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:93:        \"text\": \"The main upside risk is that the household survey can be noisy and BLS says the unemployment-rate monthly-change confidence interval is about plus or minus 0.3 percentage point near a 6.0 percent rate; a softer June household survey could round to 4.4 or 4.5 even if payrolls remain positive.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/parsed_cells.json:97:        \"text\": \"The main downside risk is continued strong labor demand: May payrolls rose 172,000, participation was steady at 61.8 percent, and the unemployment rate has held at 4.3 despite month-to-month changes in unemployment levels.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/cells.with_activity.json:3:    \"slug\": \"bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-21/2026-06-21t15-07-16z-bls-cps-unemployment-rate-2026-06/cells.with_activity.json:6:    \"title\": \"US unemployme